> find rq 1
find rq: rewrites by identities the model prices lower (cost 6 as written, under gt1030)
  cost 2   asint(x + 12582912) - 1262485504         i32(roundeven(x)) by the bits of 1.5*2^23, the add rounding x (derived)
      holds where x in [-1000, 1000], inside [-2^22, 2^22 - 1/2) and i32
      x + 1.5*2^23 lies in [2^23, 2^24), where the f32 are the integers: the add rounds x to the nearest integer, a tie to the even one, giving roundeven(x) + 1.5*2^23 exactly (below 2^22 - 1/2, roundeven(x) stays below 2^22 and the sum below 2^24)
      its bits are 0x4B000000 + (roundeven(x) + 2^22) = 0x4B400000 + roundeven(x) (exponent field 150): subtracting 0x4B400000 leaves roundeven(x)
      i32 of an integer is that integer
  cost 5   asint(roundeven(x) + 12582912) - 1262485504 the conversion i32(roundeven(x)) by the bits of 1.5*2^23 (derived)
      holds where roundeven(x) is an integer in [-1000, 1000], inside [-2^22, 2^22) and i32
      roundeven(x) + 1.5*2^23 is an integer in [2^23, 2^24), where every integer is an f32: the add does not round
      its bits are 0x4B000000 + (roundeven(x) + 2^22) = 0x4B400000 + roundeven(x) (exponent field 150, the mantissa the integer less 2^23): subtracting 0x4B400000 leaves roundeven(x)
      i32(roundeven(x)) truncates toward zero: of an integer it is that integer
  cost 5   i32(x + 12582912 - 12582912)             roundeven(x) by adding and subtracting 1.5*2^23 (derived)
      holds where x in [-1000, 1000], inside [-2^22, 2^22]; where the result is zero its sign may differ (allowed by Vulkan's default float controls, without SignedZeroInfNanPreserve)
      x + 1.5*2^23 lies in [2^23, 2^24], where the f32 are the integers: the add rounds x to the nearest integer, a tie to the even one, giving roundeven(x) + 1.5*2^23 exactly
      subtracting 1.5*2^23 leaves roundeven(x), an integer up to 2^22 in magnitude, an f32: no rounding
